<title>MEXICO: Mexico grants two local natgas distribution rights.</title>
<headline>Mexico grants two local natgas distribution rights.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Energy Regulatory Commission said Monday it granted two local companies the right to supply natural gas for their own use.</p>
<p>Gas Industrial de Monterrey in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon state and the  Sociedad de Autoabastecimiento de Gas Natural Lajat in Torreon, Coahuila state, were given official permission for 30 years to supply and use natural gas for their own needs, the commission said via the government's Official Gazette.</p>
<p>--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903</p>
